    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py:9`. The test suite passes (1 test), but that test only checks that `LABELS` is lowercase. Nothing calls `label_ticket`, and I didn't send any real API request.\n\n- **Request:** it makes one `client.messages.create` call to `MODEL` (`claude-sonnet-4-6`) with `max_tokens=5`. The system prompt asks for exactly one word from `bug, feature, question`, and the ticket text is sent as the user message.\n- **Temperature 0:** in the pinned `anthropic` 1.8.0, `create()` no longer accepts `temperature` as an argument; I checked the installed SDK source to confirm. So it goes in as `extra_body={\"temperature\": 0}`, which still sends it in every request. The API still accepts `temperature` for `claude-sonnet-4-6`. It would reject it (400 error) for Opus 4.7 and later or Sonnet 5, so if `MODEL` is moved to one of those, the labeler will need another way to stay deterministic.\n- **Return value:** it joins the text blocks of the reply, then strips and lower-cases the result. Anything that isn't in `LABELS` returns `\"question\"`.\n\nNo dependencies were added."
